          "text": "# AbstractAgent Class Summary\n\n## Overview\nThe `AbstractAgent` class serves as \"the foundation for all agent implementations in the Agent User Interaction Protocol,\" handling event processing, state management, and message history.\n\n## Configuration\n\nAgents accept an optional `AgentConfig` object with these properties:\n- `agentId`: Agent identifier\n- `description`: LLM-used agent description\n- `threadId`: Conversation thread identifier\n- `initialMessages`: Starting messages array\n- `initialState`: Initial agent state\n\n**Extending Configuration:** Create a subclass that extends `AgentConfig` and pass it to the parent constructor:\n\n```typescript\ninterface CustomConfig extends AgentConfig {\n  customOption: string\n}\n\nclass CustomAgent extends AbstractAgent {\n  constructor(config: CustomConfig) {\n    super(config)\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Core Methods\n\n| Method | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| `runAgent()` | Primary execution method returning results and new messages |\n| `subscribe()` | Registers event handlers across multiple runs |\n| `use()` | Adds middleware to the event pipeline (supports function and class-based) |\n| `abortRun()` | Cancels current execution |\n| `clone()` | Creates a deep copy |\n| `connectAgent()` | Establishes persistent connections via the `connect()` method |\n\n## Key Properties\n\n- **Public**: `agentId`, `description`, `threadId`, `messages`, `state`, `events$`\n- **Observable**: `events$` uses ReplaySubject, allowing late subscribers to receive historical events\n\n## Protected Methods for Subclassing\n\n| Method | Role |\n|--------|------|\n| `run()` | Abstract; must implement agent execution logic |\n| `connect()` | Optional; enables persistent connections |\n| `apply()` | Processes events and updates state |\n| `prepareRunAgentInput()` | Prepares execution parameters |\n| `onError()` / `onFinalize()` | Lifecycle hooks for error handling and cleanup |\n\n## Middleware Implementation\n\nAgents support chainable middleware for event stream transformation:\n\n```typescript\nagent.use(\n  (input, next) => { /* transformation logic */ return next.run(input); },\n  new CustomMiddleware()\n).runAgent()\n```",
