napshot: { todos: [...] }\n}\n\n// Incremental updates\n{\n  type: 'STATE_DELTA',\n  delta: [{ op: 'add', path: '/todos/0', value: {...} }] // RFC 6902 JSON Patch\n}\n```\n\n### 4. **Dependencies**\nInstall AG-UI packages:\n```bash\nbun add @ag-ui/core @ag-ui/client\n```\n\n### 5. **Tool Format**\nAlready compatible! Just rename:\n```typescript\n// Current (already compatible)\ninterface ToolDefinition {\n  name: string\n  description: string\n  input_schema: { type: 'object', properties: {...}, required: [...] }\n  confirmationRequired?: boolean  // Keep as custom extension\n}\n\n// AG-UI Tool type (same structure!)\ninterface Tool {\n  name: string\n  description: string\n  parameters: any  // JSON Schema (same as input_schema)\n}\n```\n\n### 6. **Migration Benefits**\n- **Ecosystem compatibility**: Works with LangGraph, CrewAI, etc.\n- **Streaming improvements**: Proper event-based streaming vs full messages\n- **State efficiency**: JSON Patch deltas instead of full state serialization\n- **Standardization**: Industry-standard protocol\n- **Future-proof**: AG-UI ecosystem support\n\n### 7. **Breaking Changes**\n- Server message format changes (events vs custom messages)\n- Client must handle event streams\n- State management API changes\n- Tool definition minor rename (`input_schema` → `parameters`)\n\n### Implementation Order\n1. Install `@ag-ui/core` and `@ag-ui/client`\n2. Create AG-UI event emitters in server\n3. Update server to emit AG-UI events for lifecycle, messages, tool calls, state\n4. Update client to parse AG-UI event streams\n5. Migrate state management to use structured state + JSON Patch\n6. Update tests\n7. Update documentation",
